1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:22,840
Full of Surprises

2
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,410
Hello. What can I do for you?

3
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:26,330
Hi. Fill 'er up.

4
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:27,680
I need a full tank.

5
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:28,800
Check the hood?

6
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:38,540
No, thanks.

7
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,200
Whereabouts are you headed?

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,460
Pete Waters's farm, near Chesterton.

9
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,270
I know it well.

10
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:49,150
Pete Waters's lived around here almost as long as I have.

11
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:51,820
How long is it going to take for me to get there?

12
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:53,630
About fifteen minutes.

13
00:00:53,630 --> 00:00:55,930
There's a shortcut--if you know it.

14
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,780
No, I don't.

15
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:00,220
Could you tell me how to use the shortcut?

16
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:02,520
Sure. You take the next left turn.

17
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,770
You'll see a stop sign.

18
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:07,010
Make a right at the stop sign.

19
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:10,470
Stay on that road, and you'll cross a blue bridge.

20
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:13,120
Then you'll see a big old red barn.

21
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:16,980
That's the back of Pete Waters's place.

22
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:22,690
That's quite a difference from the directions that Pete sent me.

23
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:26,020
Now, if you take that route, it's probably a lot simpler,

24
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:30,450
but it'll take you ten minutes longer.

25
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:34,210
OK. Let me repeat it.

26
00:01:34,210 --> 00:01:38,230
I take the next left turn to the stop sign.

27
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:42,770
Then a right across a blue bridge,

28
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:45,290
and then a big red barn.

29
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:49,890
Can't miss it.

30
00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:51,250
How much do I owe you?

31
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:56,000
Well, that'll be eighteen dollars and seventy cents.

32
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,210
No charge for the cleanup.

33
00:01:58,210 --> 00:02:01,190
It's on the house.

34
00:02:01,190 --> 00:02:02,710
Well, here's a twenty.

35
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:11,880
Ah. OK. That's a dollar and thirty cents change.

36
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:16,310
There we go ... will make twenty. Thanks.

37
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:17,870
Thank you.

38
00:02:17,870 --> 00:02:57,810
And thanks for the directions.

39
00:02:57,810 --> 00:03:00,950
This must be Pete's barn.

40
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:13,170
Turn right to the house.

41
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:13,890
Hi.

42
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:15,570
Hi. What can I do for you?

43
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,980
Is this the Pete Waters farm?

44
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,450
It is.

45
00:03:18,450 --> 00:03:19,500
I'm a friend of Pete's.

46
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,570
I'm looking for the house.

47
00:03:20,570 --> 00:03:21,750
It's just over yonder.

48
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:22,700
Keep along this road

49
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,900
till you get to the end of the fence.

50
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:24,980
You'll see the chicken house.

51
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:26,500
His house is on the left.

52
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:58,770
Well, thanks.

53
00:03:58,770 --> 00:04:00,960
"Have gone to the railroad station.

54
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,710
Back soon with a surprise.

55
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:05,510
Make yourself at home.

56
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:09,960
Have a look around. Pete.

57
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:12,190
Same old Pete Waters.

58
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:15,190
Always full of surprises.
